## Step 3: Performance Page

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet to implement the performance analytics page:

```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

# Placeholder Data (replace with real data retrieval)
dates = pd.date_range(start='2025-01-01', periods=30)
daily_pl = np.random.randint(-100, 200, size=30)
weekly_pl = np.random.randint(-500, 1000, size=4)
monthly_pl = np.random.randint(-2000, 4000, size=12)
lifetime_pl = np.cumsum(np.random.randint(-100, 200, size=100))
win_loss_ratios = {'Wins': 70, 'Losses': 30}

# Page Title
st.title("📊 Performance Analytics")

# Daily P/L (Line Chart)
st.subheader("Daily P/L")
daily_df = pd.DataFrame({"Date": dates, "P/L": daily_pl}).set_index("Date")
st.line_chart(daily_df)

# Weekly and Monthly Performance (Bar Charts)
st.subheader("Weekly and Monthly Performance")
cols = st.columns(2)
with cols[0]:
    weekly_df = pd.DataFrame({"Week": [f"Week {i+1}" for i in range(4)], "P/L": weekly_pl}).set_index("Week")
    st.bar_chart(weekly_df)
with cols[1]:
    monthly_df = pd.DataFrame({"Month": [f"Month {i+1}" for i in range(12)], "P/L": monthly_pl}).set_index("Month")
    st.bar_chart(monthly_df)

# Lifetime P/L (Cumulative Line Chart)
st.subheader("Lifetime P/L")
lifetime_df = pd.DataFrame({"Trade #": range(1, 101), "Cumulative P/L": lifetime_pl}).set_index("Trade #")
st.line_chart(lifetime_df)

# Win/Loss Ratios and Strike Rates
st.subheader("Win/Loss Ratios and Strike Rates")
st.bar_chart(pd.DataFrame(win_loss_ratios, index=["Trades"]))
```

